speechtext:
Resolved, that towards making good the supply granted to His Majesty on account of certain expenses of the public service for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1952, the following sums be granted out of the consolidated revenue fund of Canada, namely:
1.	The sum of $413,758,902.33, being one-sixth of the amount of each of the items set forth in the main estimates for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1952;
2.	The sum of $1,644,656.25, being three-quarters of the amount of items 62, 121, 204, 470 of the said estimates:
3.	The sum of $4,040,634.67, being one-third of the amount of items 39, 456, 463 of the said estimates;
4.	The sum of $536,759.17, being one-sixth of the amount of items 88, 566, 206, 209, 210 of the said estimates; and
5.	The sum of $1,322,403.33, being one-twelfth of the amount of items 86 , 386, 395, 398, 401, 411, 412, 415 , 417 , 420, 451, 458, 460, 495 of the said estimates, as set forth in the resolution concurred in this day in the committee of supply.
